      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand that passing `null` is not required as all instances are passing it and we currently dont have an instance where `removeBond` gets a non-null parentIntentReceiver, but `null` is kept here because of following reasons:\n- `removeBond` is a testStep function and as per the current design every testStep function should have the parent\u0027s intentReceiver where new actions needs to be added (internally replaced).\n- Also, since `removeBond` is creating a new IntentReceiver, it will be confusing later if we want to call it from a valid @Test function where we may miss adding such argument at that time. So its safer to do it and pass `null` so that in future if someone invokes this from a Test function, and they have a parentIntentReceiver or own IntentReceiver, they can just pass it and be mindful of the argument, else they may miss adding another argument to removeBond at that time.",
      "parentUuid": "76fc9c83_312665cc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 165,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 165,
        "endChar": 44
      },
